<title>DENMARK: Danish Radiometer 1996/97 profits down.</title>
<headline>Danish Radiometer 1996/97 profits down.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>12 months to April 30,1997</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax &amp; extra. items result 279 vs 316</p>
<p> Group net result			  187 vs 229</p>
<p> Group net turnover		    1,690 vs 1,657</p>
<p>Proposed dividend (crowns pr Dkk 20 share) 50.0 vs 10.0 NOTE - Full name of Danish medical instrument group is Radiometer A/S. It said in a statement that it expected a 1997/98 primary operating profit of 333 million crowns compared to 1996/97's 251 million crowns. The result was slightly above analysts' and Radiometer's own expectations of a 275 million crown 1996/97 pre-tax profit.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
